  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Two actually inspected Commons2025 front and2006 reverse-side pictures plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. No bespoke plans/surveys or reference-picture redistribution. Hidden architecture/finish and all heights remain approximate.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modern_photos_of_Cathedral_of_Saint_Sophia_in_Polotsk.jpg",
        "author": "Vasilii Martynov",
        "date": "2025-07-25",
        "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected front/side whole. Off-white plaster Baroque twin towers, broad lower and narrower upper open arched belfries, small round-window attics, green caps and slender decorative crosses. Shaped central stepped/curving gable with small central opening/cross; tall front arched glazing above a recessed wood portal; paired pilasters, layered cornices and selected urn/finial ornament. Rounded projecting side chapel has closed blind arches below upper windows, low green dome and small glazed lantern. Broad green metal nave roof. Fine stucco/iron details simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belarus-Polatsk-Cathedral_of_Sophia-11.jpg",
        "author": "Alex Zelenko",
        "date": "2006-07-17",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0 (multi-licensed)",
        "observed": "Actually inspected reverse-side whole: rounded tall rear apse with arched glazing and small green lantern; long nave upper wall with three large round-arched windows/pilasters above low rectangular service range. Round side chapel has lower blind arched panels, upper recessed glazing and green domical roof/lantern. Twin open tower tiers and rear shaped gable are visible. Exact current rear finish, room plan, thresholds and heights are not resolved."
      }
    ]
